  {
   "where": "main/3",
   "block": "expander",
   "proto": {
    "label": "🧠 What does this tool show?",
    "expanded": false
   }
  },
  {
   "where": "main/3/0",
   "type": "markdown",
   "value": "Think of a battery like **two water tanks** that share the same water.  \n\n- One tank is the **anode**, the other is the **cathode**.  \n- The **water** is like the lithium that moves back and forth.  \n\n💧 When you **charge** the battery, you **pump water uphill** into the anode tank.  \n⚡ When you **use** the battery, the water flows **downhill** back to the cathode.  \n\nThe **height difference** between the tanks is the **voltage** of the battery.  \nEach tank has its own **shape** (shown in the **dQ/dV plot**) that tells how much water it can hold at each level.  \n\nOver time, the tanks don't stay the same: this is **aging**.  \n- 🪣 **Anode aging (LAM-Anode)** → the anode tank shrinks.  \n- 🪣 **Cathode aging (LAM-Cathode)** → the cathode tank shrinks.  \n- 💦 **Lithium loss (LLI)** → there's simply less water to move around.  \n\nThese changes shift the tank levels and make the **OCV curve** look different.  \n\n---  \n\n### ⚙️ The knobs you can play with:  \n- **LAM-Anode** → shrink the anode tank  \n- **LAM-Cathode** → shrink the cathode tank  \n- **LLI** → reduce the total water  \n\n👉 Try the sliders and watch how the tanks, voltage, and battery health change!",
   "help": "",
   "key": null,
   "proto": {
    "body": "Think of a battery like **two water tanks** that share the same water.  \n\n- One tank is the **anode**, the other is the **cathode**.  \n- The **water** is like the lithium that moves back and forth.  \n\n💧 When you **charge** the battery, you **pump water uphill** into the anode tank.  \n⚡ When you **use** the battery, the water flows **downhill** back to the cathode.  \n\nThe **height difference** between the tanks is the **voltage** of the battery.  \nEach tank has its own **shape** (shown in the **dQ/dV plot**) that tells how much water it can hold at each level.  \n\nOver time, the tanks don't stay the same: this is **aging**.  \n- 🪣 **Anode aging (LAM-Anode)** → the anode tank shrinks.  \n- 🪣 **Cathode aging (LAM-Cathode)** → the cathode tank shrinks.  \n- 💦 **Lithium loss (LLI)** → there's simply less water to move around.  \n\nThese changes shift the tank levels and make the **OCV curve** look different.  \n\n---  \n\n### ⚙️ The knobs you can play with:  \n- **LAM-Anode** → shrink the anode tank  \n- **LAM-Cathode** → shrink the cathode tank  \n- **LLI** → reduce the total water  \n\n👉 Try the sliders and watch how the tanks, voltage, and battery health change!",
    "element_type": "NATIVE"
   }
  },
